            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Launch Planning Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Product launches can become difficult when planning begins too late,
                    responsibilities are unclear, dependencies are not tracked, or
                    teams are not aligned. A structured launch planning process helps
                    identify these issues before they affect the release.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unclear Launch Scope:</b> Without a clearly defined scope,
                    teams may continue adding requirements close to launch. Establishing
                    clear launch boundaries helps maintain focus.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unrealistic Timelines:</b> Launch dates that do not account
                    for development, testing, approvals, documentation, and operational
                    readiness can create unnecessary pressure and delays.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unclear Ownership:</b> Multiple teams may assume another team
                    is responsible for an activity. Assigning clear owners for every
                    important launch task helps prevent missed responsibilities.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Incomplete Product Readiness:</b> A product may be technically
                    developed but still require testing, documentation, monitoring,
                    training, or support preparation before launch.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Communication Gaps:</b> Poor communication can result in
                    inconsistent messaging or missed updates. A structured communication
                    plan keeps stakeholders informed throughout the launch.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unmanaged Dependencies:</b> Marketing, sales, engineering,
                    infrastructure, and support activities can depend on one another.
                    Tracking these dependencies helps reduce launch delays.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Limited Contingency Planning:</b> Unexpected technical or
                    operational issues can affect a launch. Preparing contingency
                    plans helps teams respond more effectively.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant launch planning challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

