                <h3><b>Launch Timeline and Milestone Management</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    A detailed launch timeline provides visibility into the activities
                    required to prepare and release the product. Important milestones
                    should cover development, testing, approvals, marketing preparation,
                    sales enablement, customer communication, training, and operational
                    readiness.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Teams should identify dependencies between activities and establish
                    realistic deadlines for each milestone. Regular progress reviews
                    help identify delays early and allow teams to adjust plans when
                    necessary.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Define launch milestones and target dates.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Identify task dependencies and critical activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Assign owners to important launch tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Track progress against planned milestones.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Review and adjust timelines when significant dependencies change.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

